,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>To retrieve data using multiple parameters in an <strong>Oracke APEX RESTful Servce (ORDS) GET method,</strong> you <strong>map query string parameters directly to SQL bind variables by configuring them in the handler''s parameters list.</strong></'
||'p>',
'<div style="display:flex; gap:30px; align-items:flex-start; margin-top:20px;">',
'',
'    <!-- Left Side Image -->',
'    <div style="flex:1;">',
'        <img src="#APP_FILES#GET data using multiple parameter.png"',
'             style="width:100%; max-width:900px; border:1px solid #ddd;"',
'             alt="GET data using multiple parameter">',
'    </div>',
'',
'    <!-- Right Side Steps -->',
'    <div style="flex:1;">',
'        <h4><u>Create an ORDS to fetch Data using multiple parameter</u></h4>',
'',
'        <ol>',
'            <li>Go to Oracle APEX <strong>SQL Workshop</strong>.</li>',
'            <li>Open <strong>RESTful Services</strong>.</li>',
unistr('            <li>Click <strong>Modules</strong> \2192 <strong>Create Module</strong>.</li>'),
'            <li>Enter the <strong>Module Name</strong> and <strong>Base Path</strong>, then click <strong>Create</strong>.</li>',
